course: dictionary
lesson: 15399
title: Splitting: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Splitting is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they give you clues.
explain: «Mum is splitting the pizza into eight slices.» Here splitting means cutting something into parts right now. «We are splitting the bill between the four of us.» Here splitting means sharing something between people.
explain: «The club is splitting up after the summer.» Splitting up means separating. «She had a splitting headache.» Here splitting is an adjective, and it means very bad. Always check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Splitting is the -ing form of the verb split: split, splits, split, splitting.
fact: «Splitting» means breaking or cutting something into parts, often along a line.
fact: «Splitting» can also mean sharing or dividing something between people.
fact: «Splitting up» means separating, like a group splitting up.
fact: «A splitting headache» means a very bad headache.
exercise: «We are splitting the pizza into eight slices.» What does splitting mean here? | Throwing away | Singing loudly | Painting | *Cutting into parts
exercise: «The friends are splitting the cost of the trip.» What does splitting mean here? | Hiding it under the bed | Losing count | *Sharing between people | Breaking a window
exercise: «She had a splitting headache after the game.» What does splitting mean here? | *Very bad | Very quiet | Shaped like a circle | Happy and bouncy
test: «Our club is splitting up after the summer.» What does splitting up mean? | Getting together | *Separating | Singing | Shining brightly
test: In maths, splitting 47 into 40 + 7 means what? | Rounding 47 to 50 | *Breaking 47 into parts: 40 and 7 | Taking 7 away from 47 for ever | Adding 40 and 7 to 47
exam: «She had a splitting headache after the loud concert.» What does splitting mean here? | *Very bad, as in a headache | Cutting into two equal halves | Very quiet | Sharing with friends
